WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.140
- [Elizabeth] The government
proposed and we agree

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.500
that you should spend a term
at the University there,

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.686
to learn the language.

00:00:05.686 --> 00:00:06.519
- But--

00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:07.352
- No buts.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.820
- But I'm really rather
happy at Cambridge,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.900
not to mention I've just been
cast in a wonderful role.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.733
- [Elizabeth] I know, but--

00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:16.026
- I thought no buts.

00:00:16.026 --> 00:00:17.440
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.290
- The investiture of Prince
Charles in 1969 was far more

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.210
than just a ceremony.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.050
It was a culmination of a
carefully planned strategy

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.520
to propel him into the
affections of the public.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.860
And, as we'll find out,
there's a lot more to it

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.693
than meets the eye.

00:00:30.693 --> 00:00:33.448
I'm Laura Jackson and this
is "Beneath the Crown."

00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:36.031
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.723 --> 00:00:39.470
The world nowadays is used to seeing

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.000
and hearing Prince Charles,
the Prince of Wales.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.400
It was a different story prior

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.140
to his investiture in July 1969.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.930
As a 20-year-old heir to the throne

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.650
had been a largely unknown quantity

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.940
in the eyes of the public.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.650
But then it dawned on
the struggling monarchy

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.200
and government, maybe this
shy, young man could be used

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.148
as a powerful PR tool for them both.

00:00:57.148 --> 00:01:00.010
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.010
The royal family were being left behind

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.130
by a cultural revolution that put youth

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.706
and modernity center stage
in the Swinging Sixties.

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:09.890
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.170
The Labor government was
also in trouble as the rise

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.040
of Nationalism in Wales
risked eroding their support.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.360
With the Welsh National
Party, Plaid Cymru,

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.680
having its first MP, Gwynfor
Evans, elected in 1966.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.173
- I therefore declare Gwynfor
Richard Evans duly elected.

00:01:25.173 --> 00:01:27.780
- -[Announcer] Mr. Gwynfor
Evans said that no English party

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.570
can now regard a seat
in Wales as being safe.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.960
- A plan was hatched to
introduce Prince Charles

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.370
as the Prince of Wales,

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.070
despite him taking on the
role over a decade earlier.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.570
Charles would win over the
masses, prove his Welshness,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.920
and cement his position
as the Prince of Wales,

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.240
through a televised
coronation-like ceremony

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.510
known as an investiture.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.239
- Good, that's settled then.

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:49.072
(upbeat music)

00:01:49.072 --> 00:01:50.200
- [Laura] But first,
there was the small matter

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.764
of whisking him off to
Wales to learn the language.

00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:55.340
- (speaking foreign language)

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.247
Welcome to Wales.

00:01:56.247 --> 00:01:58.400
(upbeat music)

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.560
- [Laura] In April, 1969,
Prince Charles enrolled

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.852
for one term at the University
of Wales in Aberystwyth.

00:02:04.852 --> 00:02:05.685
(upbeat music)

00:02:05.685 --> 00:02:08.360
There, he studied Welsh
culture, history, and language,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.690
ahead of the investiture
date of July the first.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.050
(upbeat music)

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.462
Time was running out to
master the native tongue.

00:02:14.462 --> 00:02:16.409
(upbeat music)

00:02:16.409 --> 00:02:18.242
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:20.356
(groaning)

00:02:20.356 --> 00:02:22.164
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:22.164 --> 00:02:23.218
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:23.218 --> 00:02:24.051
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:24.051 --> 00:02:24.884
- (speaking foreign language)
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:24.884 --> 00:02:25.717
Glide into the ooh.

00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:27.286
- I'm trying to glide into ow.

00:02:27.286 --> 00:02:28.490
- Fine.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.820
- Security fears due

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.920
to the growing Welsh
Nationalist Movement's use

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.465
of aggressive and violent methods

00:02:33.465 --> 00:02:36.030
led to 70 police officers being placed in

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.410
and around the University.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.380
Some were even deployed to work undercover

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.790
as cleaners and students.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.375
Everything seemed to be
going surprisingly smoothly.

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:44.208
(upbeat music)
(clapping)

00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:45.070
Until Prince Charles was about

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:48.443
to give his first major public
speech in Welsh in late May.

00:02:48.443 --> 00:02:50.670
(booing)

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.180
A large group of protestors
rose from their seats

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.423
to heckle him when he arrived on stage.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.970
The young Prince cut a lonely figure.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.650
But the protestors were soon driven out

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.280
by the unlikely combination of police

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.240
and elderly ladies
wielding their handbags.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.740
Charles' dignified
response drew appreciation

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.429
from the audience and calmed his nerves.

00:03:10.429 --> 00:03:15.117
(clapping)
(cheering)

00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:17.079
The speech itself went down a treat.

00:03:17.079 --> 00:03:21.155
- (speaking foreign language)

00:03:21.155 --> 00:03:23.770
(clapping)
(cheering)

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.410
- With one month to go
until his investiture,

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.140
a media blitz kicked in

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.320
as Prince Charles was
interviewed several times

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.450
across British TV and radio.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.730
It was an attempt to
launch him into the hearts

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.520
and minds of the British public,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.917
as the leader of the
next generation of royals

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:40.106
and heir to the throne.

00:03:40.106 --> 00:03:42.420
- It's a dual sort of upbringing
one has to try and do.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.471
And I think perhaps
that I'd gone to school,

00:03:45.471 --> 00:03:48.300
at University and everything,
in a much more normal way

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.520
than any of my predecessors did,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.360
has been an experiment in royal education.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.770
And of course, it has
been slightly difficult.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.130
- He came across as a
more modern, sensitive,

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.430
and relatable royal than
people were used to.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.070
He was also able to
convey his love for Wales.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.390
- When I first arrived,
I wanted to get out,

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.210
you know, as much as possible.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.510
So I went and went for drives
through the countryside

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:14.210
and walked in the mountains,
exhausted my poor policeman,

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.403
walking up and down the mountain.

00:04:15.403 --> 00:04:18.210
And I've seen a lot and
I've been very touched

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.890
by the way people have,
you know, responded,

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.430
the country people particularly.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.910
- While his relaxed manner
and humor disarmed many,

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.940
the government was concerned

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.760
that Prince Charles may be
growing a little too sympathetic

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.410
to the Welsh Nationalist cause.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.090
- I think the fatal
attitude to take is to say

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.469
that these people are wrong, you know.

00:04:36.469 --> 00:04:40.720
Therefore, you know, they
mustn't be listed to or heeded.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.570
But I think what one must
try and do is, first of all,

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.700
establish a personal
contact and actually speak

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.700
to the people and understand

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.027
what it is they're trying to get at.

00:04:49.027 --> 00:04:53.279
And a basic sympathy, I think,
is needed, an understanding.

00:04:53.279 --> 00:04:54.860
(gentle upbeat music)

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.960
- Preparations for the
investiture ceremony

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.580
at Caernarfon Castle had been
causing plenty of headaches

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:00.973
inside Buckingham Palace.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.440
Several senior members of staff

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.200
preferred a traditional approach.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.490
But Lord Snowdon, Antony Armstrong-Jones,

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.730
had been brought on board
to modernize proceedings,

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.880
including the clothing and stage design.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.940
- This looks super.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.090
I must say, an absolute plain slate.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.720
For the important thing about this is so

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.502
that cameras can come in from
behind and from in front.

00:05:20.502 --> 00:05:21.335
(exciting music)

00:05:21.335 --> 00:05:22.970
- [Announcer] At this carved Welsh slate,

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.030
impressive in its simplicity,

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.267
this was the stage where Wales
would receive its own Prince.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.640
(gentle upbeat music)

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.210
- As the big day approached,
security concerns grew.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.120
There had been numerous
bomb attempts designed

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.450
to cause chaos.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.470
But the night before the investiture,

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.900
a bomb carried by two
activists exploded prematurely,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.160
killing them both.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.795
During an enormous security
and surveillance operation,

00:05:45.795 --> 00:05:48.505
Prince Charles' investiture
went ahead as planned.

00:05:48.505 --> 00:05:49.500
(cheering)

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.293
And the crowds were out in force.

00:05:51.293 --> 00:05:52.554
(cheering)

00:05:52.554 --> 00:05:54.500
(gentle upbeat music)

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.760
The ceremony was faultless,
with the Queen investing her son

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.700
with the symbols of his office.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.613
- [Announcer] A coronet for sovereignty.

00:06:02.613 --> 00:06:05.780
(gentle upbeat music)

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.100
- [Laura] The crown
designed by Louis Osman

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.530
was controversial at the
time for its modern look.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.160
(gentle upbeat music)

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.210
It's been widely claimed
that the orb at the top was,

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:18.712
in fact, a gold-plated table tennis ball.

00:06:18.712 --> 00:06:21.860
(gentle upbeat music)

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.780
- I hope and trust that, in time,

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.040
I shall be able to offer
my own contribution.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.524
And to do that, I seek your
cooperation and understanding.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.580
(gentle upbeat music)

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.060
Speaking for myself, as a
result of my two months stay

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.460
in this country, I have
come to see far more

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.513
in the title I hold than hitherto.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:47.910
I am more than grateful to the
people of this principality

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.750
for making my brief stay
so immensely worthwhile.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.000
And for giving me such encouragement

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.330
in the learning of the language.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.730
- The reception to the ceremony

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.825
and Prince Charles' speech was rapturous.

00:06:59.825 --> 00:07:01.120
(gentle upbeat music)

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.910
A global audience of 500 million people,

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:07.455
including 19 million from the
UK, watched on television.

00:07:07.455 --> 00:07:09.760
(gentle upbeat music)

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.380
But while the investiture
itself was a success,

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:13.830
the question remained.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.350
Was Prince Charles really cut
out for the prominent role

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.010
the royal family needed him to play?

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.746
(gentle upbeat music)

00:07:20.746 --> 00:07:23.313
- I have a beating heart, a character,

00:07:23.313 --> 00:07:25.380
a mind and a will of my own.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.010
I am not just a symbol.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:29.060
I can lead not just by wearing a uniform

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.618
or by cutting a ribbon, but
by showing people who I am.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.951
(whooshing)

